implementationPlan.note:
TDD RED for the reopen repair. The step-2 spec assertions (closed vocabulary, manifest 1:1, partition completeness, labels, pinned digests, probe refs, determinism, held-out) all still hold in foundation-spec.test.ts and were NOT rewritten — QA said the design is strong.

What was missing was a spec assertion about the GATE itself, which is the defect QA found. Added packages/testkit/src/foundation/foundation-gate-coverage.test.ts (152 lines) — new file rather than growing foundation-spec.test.ts, which is already exactly at the 250 cap. It lives inside packages/testkit/src on purpose so the narrow declared command can never drop the check that guards the narrow declared command.

It reads real tool config off disk, not a prose claim:
- enumerates every .ts under BOTH owned dirs (floor >=13 so an empty scan cannot fake-pass);
- asserts each owned *.test.ts is matched by a filed gate filter, and that each filed filter covers something;
- parses packages/testkit/package.json scripts.test and pins its positional filter to exactly ["packages/testkit/src"] — if the script widens, the credited coverage must be re-derived;
- asserts vitest.config.ts still includes "tests/**/*.test.ts";
- asserts every owned file falls inside a tsconfig project that extends tsconfig.base.json, using a tsconfig-glob matcher (** spans dirs, * does not).

RED confirmed, and red for the right reason: 1 failed / 4 passed — `ENOENT ... tests\fault\foundation\tsconfig.json`. The four gate assertions that pass today are the ones already true; the one that fails is exactly QA's second blocker.
